<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Hire purchase price and extra</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>A {@itm@} costs Ksh \({@ksh(C)@}\) cash. On hire purchase you pay a deposit of \({@d@}\%\) of the cash price and \({@k@}\) monthly instalments of Ksh \({@ksh(m)@}\).</p><p>(a) Find the deposit.</p><p>Ksh [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p><p>(b) Find the hire purchase price.</p><p>Ksh [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p><p>(c) How much more than the cash price is this?</p><p>Ksh [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) Deposit \(= \dfrac{ {@d@} }{100} \times {@ksh(C)@} = {@ksh(Dep)@}\).</p><p>(b) The instalments total \({@k@} \times {@ksh(m)@} = {@ksh(km)@}\). Hire purchase price \(=\) deposit \(+\) instalments \(= {@ksh(Dep)@} + {@ksh(km)@} = {@ksh(H)@}\).</p><p>(c) \({@ksh(H)@} - {@ksh(C)@} = {@ksh(X)@}\). You use the goods now and pay more than the cash price.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[kgrp(n) := block([s, out, k], s: string(n), k: slength(s), if k < 5 then s else (out: "", while k > 3 do (out: sconcat("\\,", substring(s, k-2, k+1), out), k: k-3), sconcat(substring(s, 1, k+1), out)));
ksh(v) := block([c, w, f], c: floor(100*v+1/2), w: floor(c/100), f: c-100*w, if f = 0 then kgrp(w) else sconcat(kgrp(w), ".", if f < 10 then "0" else "", string(f)));
dd(v) := if integerp(v) then v else if integerp(10*v) then dispdp(float(v),1) else if integerp(100*v) then dispdp(float(v),2) else if integerp(1000*v) then dispdp(float(v),3) else dispdp(float(v),4);
ix: 1+rand(10);
/* Design: deposit as a percentage, then instalments. [item, cash price C, deposit %, instalments k, instalment m]. No carrying charge: the advert states the instalments. Source: adapted from SMP Book 5 (Metric), chapter 5, section 4 and Exercise H question 1. */
L: [["fridge",42000,10,12,3600],["motorbike",138000,20,18,7300],["television",33500,15,10,3200],["sewing machine",18000,10,9,2100],["water tank",27500,20,6,4100],["solar panel kit",46000,25,12,3250],["laptop",64000,15,12,5100],["gas cooker",23800,10,8,2950],["smartphone",21500,20,10,1950],["bicycle",14200,25,6,2050]];
E: L[ix];
itm: E[1]; C: E[2]; d: E[3]; k: E[4]; m: E[5];
Dep: C*d/100;
H: Dep+k*m;
X: H-C;
/* diagnostics */
km: k*m;
Hk: Dep+(k-1)*m;
Ck: C+k*m;
neg: C-H;
bal: C-Dep;
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
